# Build outputs
*.uf2
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex

# Patched ROM images from tools/build-rom.py (asm -> spliced TSPICO ROM).
# The base src/rom/TSPICO.ROM is tracked; the built variant is regenerated.
/build/

# Exception: flash_nuke.uf2 is a static, prebuilt asset (Raspberry Pi
# pico-examples flash/nuke) committed on purpose so the Web Updater can serve
# it as the "wipe the Pico" download. It is not a build output.
!web-updater/flash_nuke.uf2

# Exception: ROMs/ holds reference ROM images, not build outputs. The *.bin rule
# above (for the compiled zmakebas binary) would otherwise swallow the TS2068
# baselines that tools/romdiff.py and tools/romdisasm.sh diff against, leaving a
# fresh clone unable to run either. See docs/rom-analysis/README.md.
!ROMs/*.bin

# MicroPython compiled
*.mpy
__pycache__/

# BASIC -> TAP toolchain (tools/build-basic.sh)
# Compiled zmakebas binary + objects (vendored source under tools/zmakebas/).
tools/zmakebas/zmakebas
tools/zmakebas/*.o
# Generated .tap files compiled from basic/**/*.bas. Source is tracked; the
# .tap is built into the delivery tree (release.yml / pages.yml bundle it).
# Output paths follow the basic/ directory convention (see basic/README.md):
#   basic/SD/<rest>  -> "SD card/<rest>"   basic/<rest> -> "src/<rest>"
# Generated TAPs interleave with committed content, so each program's output is
# ignored individually as its source is migrated (git rm --cached the old .tap,
# then add its path here). The throwaway example program's output dir:
/SD card/TAP/demo/
# Migrated program outputs (add one line per program as you migrate it):
/src/assets/nofile.tap
/src/assets/romupdate.tap
/src/assets/dckupdate.tap
/SD card/readme.tap
/SD card/TAP/test/picotest1.tap
/SD card/TAP/test/picotest2.tap
/SD card/TAP/test/hdrless.tap
/SD card/TAP/picotest-s.tap
/SD card/TAP/test/factorial.tap
/SD card/TAP/test/RND WORDS.tap

# Staging dir the CI 'Stage generated .tap files' step builds before
# uploading them as the basic-taps artifact. Only appears if that step is
# run locally.
/basic-taps/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# sjasmplus listing from tools/build-rom.sh
src/rom/patches/*.lst

# Claude Code local settings (per machine: permission lists, local paths)
.claude/settings.local*.json

# docs/manual/examples: assembler output from the tests (make_tap.py rebuilds picoex.tap)
/docs/manual/examples/*.bin
/docs/manual/examples/*.sym
